 "recommendation": {
  "word": "hold",
  "why": "The picture is proved identical at every instant and width (Lean drawOne_visSame, from hidden_pause_eq; the two skipped copies are opacity 0 for the whole draw window), the breakpoint gate passes in both engines, and the animated paths per draw frame go from 3 to 1. But the saving is not visible on CI: the visible copy still forces a Layout every draw frame, so Layout and RecalculateStyles counts are equal within the pass-to-pass spread of the base, and the Layout time of the first passes is 60.4 against 63.8 ms. The lane records no per-SVG layout counts and no frame intervals, so p50, p90 and p99 are not available. Keep the flag registered and out of the preset; measure it again where frame time inside the draw windows is recorded."
